title: The Red Army's Advice
subtitle: Trotsky's officers offer the party military help.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('m_trotsky'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('m_trotsky');
Q.lw_n = Q.time >= 48 ? 1 : 0;
!}

= The Red Army's Advice

Two men in good civilian suits have come to Berlin with a letter from **Trotsky**, the People's Commissar for War. They are officers of the Red Army, and they have looked at the party's arms, its red guards and its maps. Their verdict: [? if lw_n = 1 : the party has men but not an army, weapons but not ammunition, and no plan that would survive the first day. They propose a military apparatus on Red Army lines, with sector commanders, depots and a general staff, and they ask for a date. ?][? if lw_n = 0 : a rising now would be crushed in a week. Trotsky's advice is to build in silence: cadres, depots, contacts in the Reichswehr, and to keep the party out of street fighting it cannot win. ?]

- @accept: Accept the officers and their plan.
- @money: Take the money for arms, and keep our own commanders.
- @decline: Thank them, and send them home.

@accept
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Real military preparation, and a military department the Zentrale will not fully control.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids preparing a rising.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('uprising');
Q.red_guards_arms += 6;
Q.red_guards_loyalty += 6;
Q.repression += 3;
Q.independence -= 4;
RG.ecci('trotsky', 10);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 2, 5);
!}

The officers stay. Within a month the red guards have sector commanders, couriers and depots in allotments and churchyards across the country.

@money
subtitle: 1 fund, and rifles. The red guards stay under their own district leaders.
on-arrival: {!
Q.red_guards_arms += 5;
Q.resources += 1;
RG.ecci('trotsky', 2);
!}

The officers leave a sum in dollars and a list of addresses in Hamburg where rifles can be bought off Dutch ships.

@decline
subtitle: No Russian officers in the German party. Trotsky is offended.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('trotsky', -10);
Q.independence += 5;
!}

The officers are given dinner, the thanks of the Zentrale and two tickets for the night train to Stettin, where a ship leaves for Petrograd.
